        </div>
				            <div class="columns-holder ">
                
                        <div class="raptive-video-player"></div>
                <p dir="ltr">Welcome to Wrestling Inc.'s live coverage for "WWE NXT" on November 17, 2026, coming to you live from the WWE Performance Center in Orlando, Florida! The show begins at 8 PM ET and can be streamed internationally on Netflix.</p>
<p dir="ltr">Kelani Jordan will be putting her NXT Women's Championship on the line on television for the first time since retaining against "WWE SmackDown" star Paige on the November 4 episode of "NXT" as she defends against former titleholder Kendal Grey. Jordan and Grey found themselves involved in a verbal confrontation during last Tuesday's episode of "NXT" as Grey made it clear she was looking to recapture the title.</p>
<p dir="ltr">Tony D'Angelo will be in action as he goes one-on-one with Kam Hendrix. The two men found themselves involved in a verbal confrontation with one another in the men's locker room last Tuesday, with D'Angelo's newfound rival Myles Borne watching the whole thing go down from the shadows.</p>

            </div>
            </div>
<div class="news-article"><div class="columns-holder"><section class="live-blog liveblog-container active"><div class="live-top">
    <span class="live-status">Active</span><br>
